module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.ModuleFiniteness.FiniteType
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.IdealSubmoduleFlatPullback
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.IdealSubmoduleGeneratedByOne
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.EffectiveCartierEtaleCharts
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.LocallyPrincipalChartDescent

/-!
# Stacks 083B(1) on an étale chart

Let `X` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S` contained in a big fppf site `B` and let
`Z ⊆ X` be a closed subspace which is locally principal in the sense of Stacks 083B(1): its
defining ideal sheaf `𝓘_Z ⊆ 𝒪_X` is generated by one section locally on the small étale site of
`X`.  This file proves that the closed subscheme which `Z` cuts out on an *affine étale scheme
chart* of `X` is then locally principal in the scheme sense of Stacks 01WR, that is

`IsLocallyPrincipal B S hS X Z → Stacks.Divisors.IsLocallyPrincipal (Z ×_X V ⟶ V).ker`

for every affine étale chart `V` of `X`.  This is the step which the étale-chart apparatus of
Stacks 083C supplied for invertibility of the ideal sheaf, Stacks 083B(2), and which had no
counterpart for Stacks 083B(1).

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_affine_chart_definingIdealAt_eq_span`: **every point of an
  affine étale chart of `X` is in the image of an affine étale chart over it on which the
  defining ideal of `Z` is principal.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocallyPrincipal_ker_rep_snd_of_isLocallyPrincipal`: **Stacks
  083B(1) implies local principality on every affine étale chart.**

## Implementation notes

The proof is flat descent of local principality along the étale charts of the first bullet,
carried out on the ideal subsheaf of the structure sheaf rather than on the ideal sheaf itself.
On a chart `W` over the given chart `V` the defining ideal of `Z` is principal, so the ideal
subsheaf of the inverse-image ideal sheaf on the scheme `W` is generated by one *global* section
(`Stacks.Divisors.isGeneratedByNear_unitSubmodule_of_ideal_top_eq_span`); the inverse-image
ideal subsheaf is the pullback of the ideal subsheaf of `V` because `W ⟶ V` is étale, hence flat
(`Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.pullbackIdealFlatIso`); and generation by one section near a point
descends along an arbitrary morphism of schemes through the Fitting ideals
(`AlgebraicGeometry.isGeneratedByNear_of_pullback`, Stacks 0C3F and 0C3D).  That last statement
needs the module on the base to be of finite type, which is exactly what fpqc descent of finite
type supplies from the charts (`AlgebraicGeometry.isFiniteType_of_pullback_fpqc`, Stacks 05AZ):
no Noetherian hypothesis enters anywhere.  Reading the resulting pointwise generation back as
local principality of the ideal sheaf is
`Stacks.Divisors.isLocallyPrincipal_of_forall_isGeneratedByNear`.

The charts of the first bullet come from the covering sieve that Stacks 083B(1) provides at the
chart `V` itself: a covering sieve of the small étale site is jointly surjective on the scheme
points of the chart (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_mem_sieve_scheme_point`), its members may be
shrunk to affine ones (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_affine_chart_at`) while the generating
sections restrict (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatingSectionsOverMap`), and on an affine chart a
singleton family of generating sections generates the defining ideal there on the nose
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_eq_span_definingIdealAt_of_generatingSections`).

The family of charts obtained one point at a time is an étale, hence fppf, hence fpqc covering
family of the chart scheme — jointly surjective by construction and étale on each member — and
no finiteness of the index is needed, the index being the point set of the chart scheme.

